commit 2379e12538902531dcfa7980468e0ebe19d76594
Author: kunweiz <kunweiz@local>
Date:   Sat Oct 10 11:00:00 2026 +0000

    feat: TP5 correctness hardening, necessity tooling, and perf-gap harness
    
    Core runtime (uncommitted wave since 9be06d5, per CHANGELOG Unreleased):
    
    Vulkan/collective:
    - Q publish integrity: exact F32 publisher and all Q8DOT workgroups now
      publish (payload xor, armed epoch, live word count); ready is not
      retired and Q is not folded before match. L2 statistics tag kept.
    - Legacy multi-row extent gate: per-stage row count derived from actual
      Y elements / HC width; next-bank active-row publish uses the next
      stage's rows instead of the single-row default.
    - P1 owner cleanup: tp5_p1_resources destructor drains real submissions
      before the rank command pool is destroyed; ring owners cleared while
      the pool is alive; communicator mutex released before free.
    - Native AllGather dynamic rows, BF16 router weights via F32 GEMV
      pipeline (bit-exact scores), router weight conversion kept out of
      replay definition tapes, converted-cache invalidation for strided
      uploads, meta graph view UID+base disambiguation.
    - GGUF Q2_0 type-ID 42->47 fork mapping for GSQ-RCO shards.
    - New headers: dependency ledger, Q geometry, qcheck, sparse timing,
      submit pool; shaders tp5_gather_p1, tp5_hc_norm_shared,
      tp5_predefined_add_rows.
    
    Server/sampling:
    - POSIX signal shutdown made reentrant-safe (queue locks); new
      server-signal, rerot-thinking, rerot-todo modules.
    - Greedy unique-argmax host sampling; decode-cost instrumentation
      (GGML_DECODE_COST env, default off).
    
    Tests: new CPU targets (greedy-unique-host, decode-cost, server-signal,
    dependency-ledger, q-geometry, qcheck, sparse-timing, submit-pool,
    meta-reduce-boundary) plus Python suites (gap-tools, hc-coordinate,
    hc-envelope, independent-envelope, match-model, necessity-audit,
    perf-model, necessity-certificate) and five-rank probe fixtures.
    Existing mtp-workspace/predefined/row-program/mesh/replay suites updated.
    
    Scripts: 30+ maintained tp5-*.py entries (gap-bench runner with GPU
    lock + identity capture, necessity certificate v4, hc coordinate
    prototype, paired stats, match audit/sweep) and verify-vbios-flash.sh.
    
    Verification this session: all five Python suites pass (22/6/21/19/14
    tests). CMake targets wired; ctest -N lists new CPU tests. No GPU
    measurements run in this commit.

